---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl } from '../utils/url';
const schema = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: absoluteUrl('/', Astro.site) },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy', item: absoluteUrl('/privacy/', Astro.site) },
  ],
}];
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How techwdr.com handles your data: no forms, no analytics, and YouTube only on the Videos page." schema={schema}>
  <article class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Privacy.</h1>
      <p>This site is run by David Rice. It's a simple site: no forms, no accounts, no email signup, and nothing you type in is collected.</p>
      <p><strong>Analytics.</strong> None. This site runs no analytics, no ad trackers and no LinkedIn Insight tag, and it sets no cookies of its own. If that changes, this page will be updated before it does.</p>
      <p><strong>YouTube videos.</strong> The <a href="/videos/">/videos/</a> page loads video thumbnails from YouTube's image server (i.ytimg.com), which can see your IP address and browser details. Only after you press Play does it load a YouTube player from youtube-nocookie.com, which may set cookies under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">YouTube's privacy policy</a>. Other pages don't load anything from YouTube.</p>
      <p><strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is hosted by Netlify. Like any web host, Netlify's servers automatically receive technical data when you visit, such as your IP address, so the site can be delivered and protected. Netlify processes this data under its own terms and privacy statement, and it may use its own service providers and process data in the United States or other countries. I don't use this data to track or profile you.</p>
      <p><strong>Selling data.</strong> I don't sell your personal data or share it for advertising.</p>
      <p><strong>Links out.</strong> LinkedIn, X and YouTube each have their own privacy policy once you click through.</p>
      <p><strong>Questions or requests.</strong> Email <a href="mailto:privacy@techwdr.com">privacy@techwdr.com</a>.</p>
      <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-15">October 15, 2026</time>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
